`action` is 11.1 — target is "under CRAP 50"? The ticket title says "Bring action under CRAP 50", acceptance says "each named function at or below the target". Hmm — 11.1 > 8 threshold but the rule says "new functions must be <= 8" and "the target function must go DOWN". Is `action` treated as an existing baseline function (it is in the baseline at 451.3)? "no function may go up" — action went down massively. The CI gate only fails on regressions (CRAP grew) or NEW functions over threshold 8. `action` is in the baseline, so 11.1 is fine for CI. But the ticket says "under CRAP 50" — 11.1 < 50 ✓.

Two NEW functions over 8 must be fixed:
1. `linkBlockedByPass` CC=8, cov 90% → CRAP 8.1. Need CRAP ≤ 8: either reduce CC or raise coverage to 100%. 90% cov → CRAP = 64·(0.1)³+8 = 8.064 ✓ matches 8.1. To get ≤8: cov=100% → CRAP=8.0, or CC=7. The uncovered 10%: probably the `anyLinked=false` path after a resolved-but-failed link (linkIssues throws), or catch in moveToStatus. Better: split the inner per-ref processing into a helper to reduce CC, and/or add a test where linkIssues throws. Actually simplest robust fix: extract `linkBlockedByRef(blockedKey, ref, keyMap)` helper returning boolean, and `moveToBlocked(blockedKey)` helper. That reduces linkBlockedByPass CC.

Let me count linkBlockedByPass CC=8: forEach cb: 3 (||,||) + if !blockerKey + try/catch? Apparently catch counts (+1?) + if anyLinked + try/catch → 1+3+1+1+1+1=8. Extraction:

```js
function linkBlockedByRef(blockedKey, ref, keyMap) {
    var blockerKey = resolveKey(ref, keyMap);
    if (!blockerKey) {
        console.warn('Cannot resolve blockedBy ref "' + ref + '" for ' + blockedKey);
        return false;
    }
    try {
        tracker.linkIssues(blockedKey, blockerKey, 'Blocks');
        console.log(blockerKey + ' blocks ' + blockedKey);
        return true;
    } catch (e) {
        console.warn('Failed to link ' + blockerKey + ' blocks ' + blockedKey + ':', e);
        return false;
    }

function moveToBlocked(blockedKey) {
    try {
        tracker.moveToStatus(blockedKey, STATUSES.BLOCKED);
        console.log('Set ' + blockedKey + ' to Blocked');
    } catch (e) {
        console.warn('Failed to set Blocked status on ' + blockedKey + ':', e);
    }

function linkBlockedByPass(stories, keyMap) {
    stories.forEach(function(entry) {
        var blockedKey = entry._createdKey;
        if (!blockedKey || !Array.isArray(entry.blockedBy) || entry.blockedBy.length === 0) return;
        var anyLinked = false;
        entry.blockedBy.forEach(function(ref) {
            if (linkBlockedByRef(blockedKey, ref, keyMap)) anyLinked = true;
        });
        if (anyLinked) moveToBlocked(blockedKey);
    });
}
